<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank picks up 9.05 billion rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank picks up 9.05 billion rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Wednesday it had accepted 9,050 million rupees in Short Term Federal Bonds in its weekly open market operation.</p>
<p>			Offered	 Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p>Outright sales 5,500 2,750 14.90 percent Five-month 6,300 6,300 14.65 percent Three-month 300 NIL NIL One-month NIL NIL NIL Total(million rupees)12,100 9,050</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
